>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. PPh3 is neutral. The phenoxide bears −1, S at +1 with each of two O atoms at −1 represents sulfinate; Pd(II) gives a neutral component. Both S–O bonds measure about 1.50 Å; C=N at 1.293 Å and N–N at 1.376 Å support hydrazone bond orders. Localized 29 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Checked each ligand's bond orders and formal charges against the input geometry. The atom order and coordinates of all 69 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 71 nonmetal covalent bonds: 70 within range, 1 outside range and 0 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 36–38 C-C 1.3719 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

